# Dual remote push

When the user says **push** (or asks to push changes / push all):

1. Push the current branch to **both** remotes — do not stop after one.
2. Remotes for this repo:
   - `origin` → GitLab (`gitlab.bagocitycollege.com`)
   - `github` → GitHub (`github.com/ronron475/medconnect`, Railway deploy)
3. Prefer:
   ```bash
   git push origin HEAD
   git push github HEAD
   ```
   Or equivalent for the current branch name. Use `-u` only when the branch has no upstream yet.
4. If one remote fails, still attempt the other, then report both outcomes.
5. Do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
6. Commit only when the user asked to commit; push implies pushing already-committed work (and commit first only if they also asked to commit, or said “commit and push”).
